invariant: INV-17
file: srv_kex.c
catches: srv_flight_test
reason: srv_kex_secret copies the ML-KEM shared secret into the input
  keying material and leaves the copy in h->mlkem_ss, so it outlives the
  key exchange for the rest of the handshake, and on the QUIC and record
  transports, whose handshake state lives in the session, across calls.
  test_flight_hybrid_secret and test_flight_hybrid_refusals require it
  zero once srv_derive_handshake_secrets returns, on both exits.

--- old
    CH_ASSERT(peer != NULL);
    ct_wipe(h->mlkem_ss, sizeof h->mlkem_ss);
--- new
    CH_ASSERT(peer != NULL);
